@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: OSB to Zendesk Project Name Update Integration
	Testing project sync updates in Zendesk caused by name and code changes in OSB.

Setup:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I go to the OSB admin main page

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project codes
	| ZENOSBA |
	| ZENOSBE |
	* I obtain the external IDs of the following organizations from zendesk.liferay.com
	| Zen OSB Automotive  |
	| Zen OSB Engineering |
	* I teardown organizations with the following organizationExternalIds "${staticOrganizationExternalIdList}" from zendesk.liferay.com

Scenario: Update project name and code
	Project name and code updates should reflect in zendesk.liferay.com.

	Given I create a project with the following values
	| Name         | Zen OSB Automotive |
	| Code         | ZENOSBA            |
	| Type         | Group              |
	| Industry     | Automotive         |
	| Tier         | Regular            |
	| Max Contacts | 10                 |
	| Address Line | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country      | United States      |
	| State        | California         |
	| City         | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip          | 91765              |
	| Region       | US                 |
	| Language     | English            |
	And I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	When I update a project with the code "ZENOSBA" using the following values
	| Name         | Zen OSB Engineering |
	| Code         | ZENOSBE             |
	| Industry     | Engineering         | 
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Engineering" should have the following parameters
	| Name         | Zen OSB Engineering |
	| Account Code | ZENOSBE             |
	And the support account ID of the project with the code "ZENOSBE" should match the organization external ID on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the organization "Zen OSB Engineering" should have the tag "liferay_portal"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Engineering" should have the tag "regular"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Engineering" should have the tag "us"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Engineering" should have the tag "gold"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Engineering" should have the tag "english"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Engineering" should have the tag "approved"

Scenario: Update project name and code on expired project
	Project name and code updates should reflect in zendesk.liferay.com when the project is expired.

	Given I create a project with the following values
	| Name         | Zen OSB Automotive |
	| Code         | ZENOSBA            |
	| Type         | Group              |
	| Industry     | Automotive         |
	| Tier         | Regular            |
	| Max Contacts | 10                 |
	| Address Line | 123 Main Street    |
	| Country      | United States      |
	| State        | California         |
	| City         | Diamond Bar        |
	| Zip          | 91765              |
	| Region       | US                 |
	| Language     | English            |
	And I add an order with the product "Portal Production" and support level "Gold" to the project code "ZENOSBA"
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Automotive" should be present on zendesk.liferay.com
	When I edit a project with the name "Zen OSB Automotive" and code "ZENOSBA" to have a support lifetime of "1 Minute" starting "60" days ago for the product "Portal Production"
	And I automatically have all expired projects moved to on hold status
	And I update a project with the code "ZENOSBA" using the following values
	| Name         | Zen OSB Engineering |
	| Code         | ZENOSBE             |
	| Industry     | Engineering         | 
	Then the organization "Zen OSB Engineering" should have the following parameters
	| Name         | Zen OSB Engineering |
	| Account Code | ZENOSBE             |
	And the support account ID of the project with the code "ZENOSBE" should match the organization external ID on zendesk.liferay.com
	And the organization "Zen OSB Engineering" should not have the tag "liferay_portal"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Engineering" should have the tag "regular"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Engineering" should have the tag "us"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Engineering" should not have the tag "gold"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Engineering" should have the tag "english"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Engineering" should have the tag "closed"
	And the organization "Zen OSB Engineering" should not have the tag "approved"